{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261112T181230Z_dev-04_flat_9042", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "For the 4b on-shell cascade, the AMS-02 antiproton limits approach or intersect the GCE-preferred regions at the smaller mediator-to-DM mass ratios, r = m_mediator/m_DM = 0.2–0.4. At the larger ratios shown, up to r = 1.0, the antiproton limits stay above the GCE-preferred regions. The paper draws this from the fixed-r slices in its figure of 4b panels (r = 0.2, 0.3, …, 1.0), and the statement is text only. I did not see the figure itself.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "6.3"}]}, "turns": 6, "seconds": 27.226, "tool_calls": 5, "tool_result_chars": 590259, "input_tokens": 841535, "output_tokens": 645, "parser_versions": ["3"], "ended_at": "2026-11-12T18:12:57+00:00"}
